==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|frm|palliatif}}, from {{der|en|NL.|*palliātīvus}}, from {{der|en|ML.|palliō|t=to cloak}}, from {{der|en|la|pallium||a cloak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpælɪətɪv/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpælieɪtɪv/|/ˈpæliətɪv/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-palliative.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Serving to palliate; serving to extenuate or mitigate.
# {{lb|en|medicine}} Minimising the progression of a [[disease]] and relieving [[undesirable]] [[symptoms]] for as long as possible, rather than attempting to cure the (usually [[incurable]]) disease.

====Derived terms====
* [[ palliative care]]

